# modules/image/checks-config.rules - the container-image module's own
# per-owner registry (rules/RULE-FORMAT.md §9's `checks-<name>.rules` row,
# docs/FOUNDATION.md tension 29) for `IMAGE-CFG-RUNS_AS_ROOT-01` (IMG-06,
# data/scoursh-image-scan-design/report.md §4.1's IMAGE-CFG-* row).
#
# `script: config.sh` - modules/image/config.sh is the owning driver
# (`image_check_root_user`), a NEW file rather than an addition to
# distro/apk.sh or engine.sh: this check is DISTRO-AGNOSTIC (report.md
# §4.4 - it reads the image's own CONFIG blob, not a Dockerfile and not any
# apk-specific data), so it belongs to neither this module's apk-specific
# driver nor a future dpkg/rpm one.
#
# `tags: passive` / `tags: quick` - reads one already-extracted local
# config blob, no network call, no mutation - the identical reasoning
# modules/image/checks-apk.rules and checks-advisories.rules already give
# for their own tags.
#
# `severity: medium` - report.md §4.1's own table value, one step below
# `IAC-DOCKER-ROOT_USER-01`'s `high`: this check confirms the EFFECTIVE
# runtime user from the built artifact, but (unlike source review) it
# cannot see whether a later `docker run --user` override at deploy time
# already corrects it, so it is reported at a slightly more conservative
# severity than its source-side counterpart.
#
# `coverage-scope: image-id` - the only legal value for the `IMAGE` module
# (rules/RULE-FORMAT.md §9.5.1's frozen table).

id: IMAGE-CFG-RUNS_AS_ROOT-01
title: Image config declares no non-root USER - the effective runtime user is root
script: config.sh
severity: medium
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-250
owasp: A04:2021
tags: passive
tags: quick
coverage-scope: image-id
remediation: Add (or fix) a non-root USER in the Dockerfile that built this
  image's final stage, or in whichever base image sets it, then rebuild and
  re-scan. A base-image bump alone can change the effective user without
  any Dockerfile line changing, so re-check this after any FROM tag/digest
  bump too. This is the built-artifact counterpart to
  IAC-DOCKER-ROOT_USER-01, which reads only one Dockerfile's own USER
  instruction and cannot see the effective user across a base image or a
  multi-stage build.
references: data/scoursh-image-scan-design/report.md
references: CWE-250
references: https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design/
